 "intro": "Off Cape Myonessus, on the coast of Asia Minor, 190 BC. Antiochus’s fleet under Polyxenidas has come out to stop the Roman army crossing to Asia. You are the praetor Lucius Aemilius Regillus, with Roman and Rhodian ships.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s account, the Roman and Rhodian fleet of about 80 ships met Polyxenidas’s 89 off Myonessus. The Seleucids tried to outflank the Roman line, but the Romans broke their centre and the Rhodians, using fire pots hung from poles at their bows, drove off their wing. About 42 Seleucid ships were sunk or taken. The Roman army then crossed to Asia and won at Magnesia. The other choices are what-ifs.",
